thinking
**Reviewing file content**

I think I need to review the changed file content because there might be potential issues. I should inspect it and maybe use jq to get summary counts. It could be helpful to adjust the candidate lists if needed. Perhaps I could run a quick script to ensure all relatedFicheIds are a subset of candidateFicheIds, that the candidate count is less than or equal to 3, and check that reasons are not empty. I'll use a Node script for this.
codex
The state refresh picked up the batch and increased `csp` linked items by 20. I’m doing one final contract check on the batch payload itself: candidate count, related-within-candidate, and non-empty reasons.
exec
/bin/zsh -lc "node - <<'NODE'
const fs = require('fs');
const p = 'data-init/suggestions/question-fiche-links.csp.r003.json';
const data = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p, 'utf8'));
for (const item of data.items) {
  if (item.candidateFicheIds.length > 3) throw new Error("'`${item.questionId}: too many candidates`);
  if (!item.reasons.length) throw new Error(`${item.questionId}: missing reasons`);
  for (const id of item.relatedFicheIds) {
    if (!item.candidateFicheIds.includes(id)) throw new Error(`${item.questionId}: related id not in candidates`);
  }
}
